pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The positive half of the slack-overflow pair, and the control that pins causation to the
% WRAP rather than to the magnitude of the numbers. These degrees are ONE larger than the
% ones in `incorrect/version3/rup_propagation_slack_overflow_formula_borne.opb`, which puts
% the slack at exactly i64::MAX: no overflow, so the propagator never claimed these rows
% propagate, and the false `rup >= 1 ;` was rejected even before the fix. Here the same
% formula is proved SATISFIABLE, which it is — every assignment is a model.
f 2 ;
sol ~x1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
